94139535599 true] [17592186356893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356893 1111 #uuid "7749ee96-a62d-556b-bbdc-70fd94edfaa4" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356894 1034 "\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)}{x-2}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356894 1111 #uuid "d5907140-1688-57f7-ac12-799aa6a208f0" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356895 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-2)}{2x-1}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356895 1111 #uuid "d4bc8604-6712-5d7e-b19f-8be9913c9103" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356896 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{2x-2}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356896 1111 #uuid "709d1deb-a452-5e50-af70-36c13ca7d3c9" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356897 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-4}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356897 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356897 1111 #uuid "a243c93e-d258-5f2e-b8ab-62e5253595e4" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356898 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356899 13194139535599 true] [17592186356898 1089 "q-118389" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356898 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535599 true] [17592186356898 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068172/assets/37434a61262f829160fc2b19fcadb67745a024d589cd1ce318ca4ab90d6ab2d9.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ on the curve $y=\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{x}}$ that is closest to the point $(2,0)$ satisfies the equation\n\n$$\n2x-3-=0.\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356898 1113 #uuid "f0024a60-f6e5-5b56-9272-60dda6ebe058" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356898 1145 "Let's consider the *squared* distance $S$ between $(2,0)$ and a general point $P(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x,y) & =(x-2)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe require that the point $P$ lies on the curve $y=\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+{y}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+{(\\frac{x+1}{\\sqrt{x}})}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4x+4+x+2+\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-3x+\\frac{1}{x}+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the minimum distance, we take the first derivative of $S(x)$ and equate it to zero. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x)=2x-3-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356900 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356901 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356902 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356903 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356904 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1041 "selection" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356901 13194139535599 true] [17592186356899 1110 #uuid "562e643b-aa2e-58a2-ab6f-f4a00594d324" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356900 1034 "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356900 1111 #uuid "904f4034-f46d-54e4-8eeb-e353c591d0e8" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356901 1034 "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356901 1111 #uuid "0e2f437e-7399-55cf-ad26-b5fe4875ab88" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356902 1034 "\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356902 1111 #uuid "bebde464-721f-53b0-a0c3-f508baa5c5bb" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356903 1034 "\\frac{1}{2x}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186