rst derivative of $S(x)$ and equate it to zero. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x)=2x+2{log}_{2}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356961 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356962 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356963 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356964 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356965 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1041 "selection" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1104 #edb/ref 17592186356961 13194139535599 true] [17592186356960 1110 #uuid "2266363b-fa3c-5ec3-818f-fdb3cd80e4c5" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356961 1034 "\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356961 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356961 1111 #uuid "3ca22505-7493-5625-b2e5-91f2d3ea229d" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356962 1034 "{ln}^{2}⁡x" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356962 1111 #uuid "d29aa882-ffe2-5c8e-9af5-3eba09f685a8" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356963 1034 "\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356963 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356963 1111 #uuid "f67884e0-d673-5a66-a3e7-4b29bb24482a" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356964 1034 "\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡x}{x{log}_{2}⁡2}" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356964 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356964 1111 #uuid "60aae3cc-7c90-5068-865b-912ffecdc4f9" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356965 1034 "2x{log}_{2}⁡x" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356965 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535599 true] [17592186356965 1111 #uuid "58fc8055-430a-5bdf-b935-ab43ced09a5f" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356966 1017 #edb/ref 17592186356967 13194139535599 true] [17592186356966 1089 "q-49054" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356966 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535599 true] [17592186356966 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14068172/assets/47849c87c3c8cf9008b6531e740c6fc57058905cf17e31e4c93c479f337f0fbd.png)\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the point $P$ on the curve $y={e}^{x}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}$ that is closest to the point $(1,0)$ satisfies the equation\n\n$$\n2x-2+=0.\n$$\n\n \nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356966 1113 #uuid "eb0ef12c-9b61-582b-acd5-7493f7def056" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356966 1145 "Let's consider the *squared* distance $S$ between $(1,0)$ and a general point $P(x,y):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(x,y) & =(x-1)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x+1+{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe require that the point $P$ lies on the curve $y={e}^{x}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={x}^{2}-2x+1+{y}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x+1+{({e}^{x}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-2x+1+{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the minimum distance, we take the first derivative of $S(x)$ and equate it to zero. This gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}^{′}(x)=2x-2+{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =0 \\\\ 2x-2+{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535599 true] [17592186356967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356968 13194139535599 true] [17592186356967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356969 13194139535599 true] [17592186356967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356970 13194139535599 true] [17592186356967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356971 13194139535599 true] [17592186356967 1000 #edb/ref 17592186356972 13194139535599 true] [17592186356967 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535599 true] [17592186356967 1041 "selection" 13194139535599